---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const media = '/media/observer-screenshot';
---
<section class="observer-showcase wrap" id="saved-observer-view" aria-labelledby="observer-title" data-observer-showcase>
  <header class="observer-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">A recorded observer image</p><h2 id="observer-title">See the page<br /><em>after the click.</em></h2></div><p>The click returned its normal result. Separately, the observer captured that page for the person reviewing the work. PanelForge’s actual tool card displayed the saved screenshot and opened it at full size.</p></header>
  <p class="observer-scope">Actual browser action and PanelForge viewer, with a <strong>fictional local page and saved conversation.</strong> Object storage was a local test service. <strong>No model ran.</strong></p>
  <div class="observer-evidence">
    <figure class="observer-card"><img src={`${media}/tool-card.png`} width="420" height="364" alt="Actual desktop tool-card detail: Successfully clicked on the element, Page after this step, and the fictional checklist showing Ready." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Actual desktop tool-card detail from the saved UI review, cropped for readability. The linked observer image retains its original bytes.</figcaption><a href={`${media}/tool-card.png`}>Inspect the card detail at full size <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></figure>
    <dl class="observer-outputs" aria-label="Two separate outputs from the saved check">
      <div data-observer-client><dt>Tool response</dt><dd><p>The original MCP action response was forwarded unchanged. No observer image or reference was added.</p><blockquote>Successfully clicked on the element</blockquote><p class="observer-output-note">Selected actual tool output. The screenshot supplies the visible page state.</p></dd></div>
      <div data-observer-human><dt>Human view</dt><dd><p>A separate <strong>1024 × 768</strong> screenshot showed the checklist’s <strong>Ready</strong> state. Its bytes matched the image served to the tool card and opened in the real viewer.</p><a href={`${media}/observer.webp`}>Open the actual observer image <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><p class="observer-output-note">A saved image, not a new browser action.</p></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <details class="observer-method" data-observer-method><summary>Source and test boundaries <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
    <p>The main proof made one observed click and one upload. A separate early plain MCP gate checked clicking and capture. Unchanged Metaclaude <strong>v0.1.41</strong> proxy/helper and <strong>chrome-devtools-mcp 1.10.1</strong> ran in Chrome for Testing 156.0.8078.4. The saved result was checked on 15 October 2026.</p>
    <p>PanelForge <strong>web-v10.20.97</strong> used its actual tool card, observation endpoint, BorgStashReader and PhotoSwipe viewer. A synthetic completed tool row preserved the actual tool identity, arguments and result text. The surrounding conversation and one-second display timing were authored fixture metadata, not agent output or measured click duration.</p>
    <p>A local fake HTTPS object receiver and filesystem-backed storage adapter replaced R2. The guest endpoint returned 401; the admin endpoint returned 200 after expansion. The card and lightbox decoded the same pixels as the stored WebP. This does not test real R2 authentication, engine/archive ingestion or an installed Claude hook lifecycle.</p>
    <p>No Claude or Codex CLI, model or provider inference ran. The measured statement is unchanged MCP client response bytes; the human client requested its image separately. This is not a model-input comparison during inference or a general pass/fail check for the page.</p>
    <p>Denied preference writes produced a fetch error, a decorative splash was absent, and no provider was configured. Those retained fixture limits did not prevent the selected observation and viewer result.</p>
    <p>The card detail is an exact crop of a frame from the later review of the completed observation. No pixels were regenerated. The linked WebP is the unchanged 11,426-byte observer image, including its standard sRGB metadata.</p>
    <a href={`${media}/receipt.json`}>Read the concise observer receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
  </div></details>
</section>
<style>
.observer-showcase{padding-block:24px 44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:26px}.observer-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:24px 56px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:22px}.observer-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4.3vw,4rem);line-height:1.08}.observer-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.observer-intro>p{max-width:500px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.observer-scope{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;padding:16px 20px;background:#edf0e4;border-left:3px solid var(--forest);margin-bottom:30px;max-width:1000px}.observer-scope strong{font-weight:600}.observer-evidence{display:grid;grid-template-columns:420px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px 64px;align-items:start;margin-bottom:30px}.observer-card{margin:0;min-width:0}.observer-card img{display:block;width:420px;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #8d9b82;border-radius:4px;background:#172221}.observer-card figcaption{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-top:14px}.observer-card a,.observer-outputs a,.observer-method a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:46px;font-size:15px;margin-top:4px}.observer-showcase :global(.ui-icon){width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0}.observer-outputs{margin:0;min-width:0}.observer-outputs>div{padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.observer-outputs>div:first-child{padding-top:0;border-top:0}.observer-outputs dt{font-size:22px;line-height:1.4;font-weight:550;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin-bottom:13px}.observer-outputs dd{margin:0}.observer-outputs p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);max-width:650px}.observer-outputs blockquote{margin:17px 0 10px;padding:15px 18px;border-left:2px solid var(--forest);background:#e9eddf;font:16px/1.8 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere;color:var(--forest-dark)}.observer-outputs .observer-output-note{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;margin:6px 0 0}.observer-method{border-block:1px solid var(--line)}.observer-method>summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;min-height:58px;padding:14px 4px;font-size:16px;font-weight:550;cursor:pointer}.observer-method[open]>summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.observer-method>div{padding:8px 0 22px}.observer-method p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted);max-width:970px;margin-bottom:15px}.observer-showcase :is(a,summary):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:1000px){.observer-evidence{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,420px) minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px}.observer-intro{gap:28px}.observer-outputs p{font-size:16px}}
@media(max-width:760px){.observer-showcase{padding-block:12px 34px}.observer-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.observer-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,8vw,3.2rem)}.observer-intro>p{font-size:16px;max-width:none}.observer-scope{padding:14px 16px}.observer-evidence{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:26px}.observer-card{max-width:420px}.observer-outputs dt{font-size:23px}.observer-outputs p{font-size:16px}.observer-outputs blockquote{font-size:15px}.observer-method>summary{font-size:15px}}
</style>
